# Nautilus DevOps — Multi-Environment AWS S3 Infrastructure

This repository contains the Infrastructure as Code (IaC) configuration used by the Nautilus DevOps team to provision and manage three environment-specific AWS S3 buckets (`Dev`, `Staging`, and `Prod`) with lifecycle archiving, tag drift protection, and public-read object policies.

---

## Architecture & Resource Summary

| Environment | Bucket Name | Owner | `Name` Tag | `Backup` Tag | Glacier Lifecycle (30 Days) | Public Read Policy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Dev** | `datacenter-dev-bucket-585580237` | Alice | Yes | No | Disabled | Enabled (`s3:GetObject`) |
| **Staging** | `datacenter-staging-bucket-585580237` | Bob | Yes | `true` | Enabled (`MoveToGlacier`) | Enabled (`s3:GetObject`) |
| **Prod** | `datacenter-prod-bucket-585580237` | Carol | No | `true` | Enabled (`MoveToGlacier`) | Enabled (`s3:GetObject`) |

